---
import DocsNav from "../../components/DocsNav.astro";
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import { repositoryUrl } from "../../data/site";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Integration | Loom Kernels"
  description="Build the native wheel and connect Loom Kernels to PyTorch or vLLM."
  active="Integration"
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Integration</p>
    <h1>Adapters translate. Engines decide.</h1>
    <p>
      Loom borrows framework tensors and the current CUDA stream. The adapter
      rejects unsupported contracts before dispatch.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="docs-layout">
    <DocsNav active="Integration" />
    <article class="prose">
      <h2>Build the native wheel</h2>
      <pre><code>python3 -m venv .venv-wheel
.venv-wheel/bin/pip install \
  'setuptools&gt;=80,&lt;82' 'wheel&gt;=0.45' build 'torch&gt;=2.10,&lt;2.12'

CUDA_HOME=/usr/local/cuda-13.1 LOOM_CUDA_ARCHS=90 \
  .venv-wheel/bin/python python/build_wheel.py \
  --cuda-home /usr/local/cuda-13.1 --archs 90 --wheel-dir dist</code></pre>
      <p>
        The ABI12 wheel packages two native libraries and a build manifest. The
        H20 matrix qualifies it, but no package index publishes it.
      </p>

      <h2>Call PyTorch</h2>
      <pre><code>from loom_kernels import categorical_sample, moe_combine, moe_permute

permuted, offsets, inverse, assignments = moe_permute(
    hidden, expert_ids, num_experts=64,
)
expert_output = engine_grouped_gemm(permuted, offsets)
output = moe_combine(expert_output, weights, inverse, offsets)

token_ids = categorical_sample(probabilities, rng_state)</code></pre>
      <p>
        The engine still owns grouped GEMM, probability policy, allocations,
        and request lifecycle. Loom owns the admitted movement or sampling call.
      </p>

      <h2>Enable vLLM routes</h2>
      <pre><code>from loom_kernels.vllm import (
    register_vllm_categorical_sample,
    register_vllm_moe_movement,
)

register_vllm_categorical_sample()
register_vllm_moe_movement()</code></pre>
      <p>
        Registration is explicit. Each route checks vLLM version, shape,
        dtype, layout, and semantics. Rejected calls stay on vLLM's native path.
      </p>

      <div class="doc-note">
        <strong>No hidden conversion.</strong>
        <p>
          Loom does not copy, cast, reshape, or change sampling policy to make a
          call eligible.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>Qualified versions</h2>
      <table class="operator-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Component</th><th>Range</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>CUDA and GPU</td><td>CUDA 13.1, SM90, NVIDIA H20</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Python</td><td>3.11</td></tr>
          <tr><td>PyTorch</td><td>2.10 to 2.11</td></tr>
          <tr><td>vLLM</td><td>0.24 to 0.25</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <p>
        Read the <a href={`${repositoryUrl}/blob/main/python/README.md`}>Python guide</a>
        for install details and the
        <a href={`${repositoryUrl}/blob/main/docs/guides/vllm-ir-provider.md`}>vLLM provider guide</a>
        for every route and fallback contract.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
